WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.741
A tenant is a separate site that runs inside the same Orchard Core application.

00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:09.925
In this video you add a tenant from the administration of the Default

00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:15.280
tenant, the first site of the application, finish its setup, and open the site it creates.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.067
Adding a tenant takes two stages.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.526
First you create it:

00:00:23.526 --> 00:00:27.732
the Default tenant saves the name, the address and the presets of the

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:31.210
tenant, and the tenant waits in the Uninitialized state.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.258
Then you set it up.

00:00:33.258 --> 00:00:36.581
The Setup screen asks for the name of the site and a super

00:00:36.581 --> 00:00:39.437
user, prepares the database, and runs the recipe.

00:00:39.437 --> 00:00:41.150
The tenant ends up Running.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.432
The Tenants feature is available on the Default tenant only.

00:00:45.432 --> 00:00:51.640
Its Multi-Tenancy menu appears for users with the Manage tenants permission, which the Administrator role has.

00:00:55.876 --> 00:01:01.000
In the administration of the Default tenant, open Multi-Tenancy, Tenants.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.660
The list holds one tenant, Default.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.216
Select Add Tenant.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.584
The Create Tenant form starts with the Name.

00:01:08.584 --> 00:01:09.809
Type Maplewood.

00:01:09.809 --> 00:01:15.527
The name identifies the tenant, it can't contain spaces, and it can't be changed afterwards.

00:01:15.981 --> 00:01:19.131
Category and Description are for your own use.

00:01:19.131 --> 00:01:23.130
The list shows both, and a Category filter narrows the list.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.281
Let's enter Customers and a short description.

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:31.330
Url Prefix and Hostname decide which requests reach the tenant.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:35.981
A prefix adds a segment to the address, and a hostname gives the

00:01:35.981 --> 00:01:37.841
tenant its own domain.

00:01:37.841 --> 00:01:40.166
Type maplewood as the prefix.

00:01:40.621 --> 00:01:44.827
Two tenants can't share the same combination of prefix and hostname.

00:01:44.827 --> 00:01:49.261
The Default tenant has neither, so Maplewood needs at least one of them.

00:01:49.728 --> 00:01:52.005
Recipe lists the setup recipes.

00:01:52.005 --> 00:01:57.236
Choose Blog to preset the choice, so the Setup screen doesn't ask for a recipe.

00:01:57.236 --> 00:02:01.298
Left on Select a recipe, whoever sets up the tenant chooses.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.548
Database Presets say where the tenant keeps its data.

00:02:05.548 --> 00:02:10.698
With Sql Server, MySql or Postgres, you can enter a Connection string, and

00:02:10.698 --> 00:02:14.110
a Table Prefix lets tenants share one database.

00:02:14.568 --> 00:02:19.455
Sqlite needs neither, so the Connection string, Table Prefix and Table Schema fields

00:02:19.455 --> 00:02:21.355
disappear when you choose it.

00:02:21.355 --> 00:02:25.047
You can also leave the type on None, and then the Setup screen

00:02:25.047 --> 00:02:26.568
asks for the database.

00:02:27.019 --> 00:02:30.164
Create saves the tenant and returns to the list.

00:02:30.164 --> 00:02:34.649
Create & Setup saves it and opens its Setup screen straight away, which

00:02:34.649 --> 00:02:36.279
a later chapter shows.

00:02:40.499 --> 00:02:46.505
Maplewood appears with its category, its description, the Sqlite database, the Blog recipe

00:02:46.505 --> 00:02:48.632
and the state Uninitialized.

00:02:48.632 --> 00:02:53.199
Uninitialized means the tenant is saved, but its setup has not run.

00:02:53.725 --> 00:02:57.444
Setup and the name of the tenant both open its Setup screen.

00:02:57.444 --> 00:03:01.276
Their link carries a token that is valid for 24 hours, and the

00:03:01.276 --> 00:03:03.980
Setup screen answers Not Found without it.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.685
Loading the list again makes a fresh link.

00:03:10.985 --> 00:03:12.997
Select Setup in the Maplewood row.

00:03:12.997 --> 00:03:15.914
The first question is What is the name of your site?

00:03:15.914 --> 00:03:17.322
Type Maplewood Bakery:

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:19.485
it is the default title of the pages.

00:03:19.971 --> 00:03:26.135
This screen has no Recipe and no database questions, because the tenant already has those presets.

00:03:26.135 --> 00:03:30.461
Without them, the screen would ask for the recipe and the database.

00:03:30.927 --> 00:03:35.478
Default Time Zone sets how dates and times are displayed and edited in the site.

00:03:35.478 --> 00:03:39.447
It starts as the time zone of the server, and you can choose another.

00:03:39.912 --> 00:03:44.517
The Super User is the first user of the tenant, and has all the rights.

00:03:44.517 --> 00:03:49.003
Enter a User Name, an Email and a Password, and confirm the password.

00:03:49.003 --> 00:03:52.412
Use this user only for setup and disaster recovery.

00:03:52.882 --> 00:03:55.665
The Finish Setup button starts the work.

00:03:55.665 --> 00:04:00.324
Setup prepares the database and runs the recipe, and while it runs, the

00:04:00.324 --> 00:04:04.862
tenant is Initializing and answers requests with Service Unavailable.

00:04:05.338 --> 00:04:07.033
Let's select Finish Setup.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:10.739
When Setup is done, the browser opens the home page of the site.

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:14.075
It is a blog with a sample post, and the name you entered

00:04:14.075 --> 00:04:15.398
appears at the top.

00:04:19.665 --> 00:04:25.034
In the list, Maplewood is Running, and its row offers View, Disable, Reload

00:04:25.034 --> 00:04:27.420
and Features instead of Setup.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:31.065
A separate video covers managing running tenants.

00:04:31.518 --> 00:04:32.628
Select View.

00:04:32.628 --> 00:04:34.849
The site opens in another tab.

00:04:34.849 --> 00:04:39.291
A tenant is a separate site with its own content, theme and users,

00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:42.438
although it runs inside the same application.

00:04:42.898 --> 00:04:47.811
Open the Admin address of Maplewood, which is its prefix followed by Admin.

00:04:47.811 --> 00:04:52.299
It leads to a sign-in page, because Setup creates the super user but

00:04:52.299 --> 00:04:54.058
doesn't sign anyone in.

00:04:58.258 --> 00:05:03.000
Create & Setup saves the tenant and goes straight to its Setup screen,

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.809
so the list is skipped.

00:05:04.809 --> 00:05:10.548
Let's add Riverside with a prefix, the Blog recipe and Sqlite, the same way as before.

00:05:11.012 --> 00:05:12.692
Select Create & Setup.

00:05:12.692 --> 00:05:17.312
The tenant is saved, and its Setup screen opens straight away, with the

00:05:17.312 --> 00:05:19.412
token already in the address.

00:05:19.412 --> 00:05:23.132
It is the same screen, so the setup continues as before.

00:05:25.132 --> 00:05:27.045
Adding a tenant takes two stages:

00:05:27.045 --> 00:05:30.282
you create it from the Default tenant, then you set it up on

00:05:30.282 --> 00:05:31.607
its own Setup screen.

00:05:31.607 --> 00:05:32.882
Thanks for watching.

